ligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we normalize $\\mathbf{v}_1$ and $\\mathbf{v}_2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nq_{1} &= \\frac{v_{1}}{‖v_{1}‖} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\nq_{2} &= \\frac{v_{2}}{‖v_{2}‖} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute $R$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nR &= Q^{T}A \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{6} & 2\\sqrt{6} \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following QR factorization of $A$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nq_{11} \\cdot r_{12} = \\left(\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\right) \\cdot \\left({2\\sqrt6}\\right) = 2\n$$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 false] [17592186133613 1074 "Let $\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2$ be the columns of $A.$\n\nFirst, we find an orthonormal basis of $\\textrm{Col}(A)=\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2\\}$ using the Gram-Schmidt process.\n\n**Step 1**. We set ![](images/9c/9c487a6edad04f5c2d192eab5c5cdacbcf3414cbc3c2ea556aca7fa54aec146c.png)\n\n**Step 2**. We find the vector $\\mathbf{v}_2$ orthogonal to $\\text{Span}\\{\\mathbf{v}_1\\}$ using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}{a}_{2} \\\\  & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{12}{6}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we normalize $\\mathbf{v}_1$ and $\\mathbf{v}_2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{