er the action of $A-2I:$\n\n$$\n(A-2I)v=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]={{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{w}\\ne 0\n$$\n\n- Since we got a nonzero vector in the last step, we now compute the image of $w$ under the action of $A-2I:$\n\n$$\n(A-2I)w=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the following chain of maps:\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{v}\\overset{A-2I\\,}{\\to }{{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{w}\\overset{A-2I\\,}{\\to }{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{0}\n$$\n\nHere, we see that $A-2I$ maps $v$ to $0$ in $2$ steps.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$\\,$ *$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ of $A.$*\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362682 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362683 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362682 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362684 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362682 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362685 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362682 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362686 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362682 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362687 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362682 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362682 1077 "selection" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362682 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362687 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362682 1080 #uuid "50e44f68-8e03-5772-829b-5a09815b3ae9" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362683 1081 "None of the statements are true" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362683 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362683 1084 #uuid "8b0fb635-b2b2-5e34-ac62-08f8f2e8ae69" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] 