he value of $f(2).$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362817 1072 #uuid "b44c043c-3403-5cd7-8682-20a3edded75a" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362817 1074 "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $a=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)(x-0) \\\\  & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that $f(0)=3,$ and since ${f}^{′}(x)=(5x-3)^{2}(4x-2)^{4},$ then ${f}^{′}(0)=(5(0)-3)^{2}(4(0)-2)^{4}=144.$ So, the tangent line approximation is given by\n\n$$\nL(x)=3+144x.\n$$\n\nNow, we can approximate $f(2)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=2.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) & ≈L(2) \\\\  & =3+144(2) \\\\  & =3+288 \\\\  & =291.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362818 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362819 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362818 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362820 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362818 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362821 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362818 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362822 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362818 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362823 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362818 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362818 1077 "selection" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362818 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362823 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362818 1080 #uuid "17205626-0c95-53d9-b874-0c1ce0f37d36" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362819 1081 "285" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362819 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362819 1084 #uuid "f709fba9-e824-54ae-a35e-95151d935a10" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362820 1081 "288" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362820 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362820 1084 #uuid "3fd58eb4-73e3-5355-bf3e-faa3fc84d34c" 131941395