5 true] [17592186362886 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362886 1071 "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.2$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0$ | $0.25$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.1$ | $0$ | $0.15$ |\n\nCompute $P(0\\le Y\\le 1\\,|\\,X=3)$ given that the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362886 1072 #uuid "dcd58ecc-34a7-5fb8-abf6-ad622f5c0130" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362886 1074 "By the multiplication law for conditional probability, the required conditional probability is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0\\le Y\\le 1\\,|\\,X=3) & =\\frac{P((0\\le Y\\le 1),X=3)}{P(X=3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(X=3,(0\\le Y\\le 1))}{P(X=3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(X=3,Y=0)+P(X=3,Y=1)}{P(X=3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(3,0)+f(3,1)}{{f}_{X}(3)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal distribution of $X.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(3) & =f(3,0)+f(3,1)+f(3,2) \\\\  & =0.1+0+0.15 \\\\  & =0.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, we have that $f(3,0)=0.1$ and $f(3,1)=0.$ \n\nFinally, substituting our values into our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0\\le Y\\le 1\\,|\\,X=3) & =\\frac{f(3,0)+f(3,1)}{{f}_{X}(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.1+0}{0.25} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.1}{0.25} \\\\  & =0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362887 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362888 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362887 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362889 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362887 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362890 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362887 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362891 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362887