 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362995 1071 "Evaluate the integral of the function $f(x,y)=x{y}^{2}$ along the polar curve $r=2$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362995 1072 #uuid "05fbe250-8eb4-5b81-83cc-08a815c1aec0" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362995 1074 "In polar coordinates, the formula for the line integral is given by\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe connection between polar and Cartesian coordinates gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta , \\\\ y & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, along our curve, we have $x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ and $y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $, where $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=x{y}^{2}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) & =(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2} \\\\  & =8{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(2)=0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}8{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =16{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ $\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =16{\\int }_{0}^{1}{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}{u}^{3}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}({1}^{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362996 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362997 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362996 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362998 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362996 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362999 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362996 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363000 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362996 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363001 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362996 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362996 1077 "selection" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362996 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362997 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362996 1080 #uuid "c54a12c4-ac53-57bf-ac59-6e5331dff070" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362997 1081 "\\frac{16}{3}" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362997 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362997 1084 #uuid "3978ab12-c2c3-556b-8b3e-3e2439bb98af" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362998 1081 "16" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362998 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362998 1084 #uuid "921abcc9-664f-5748-a32a-b8cb3a3a1679" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362999 1081 "8" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362999 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186362999 1084 #uuid "55926885-53a5-5ed5-b872-7944d1c6177d" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363000 1081 "\\frac{4}{3}" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363000 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363000 1084 #uuid "87181d2e-ae8e-5568-bad0-b0d06ff451c4" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363001 1081 "4" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363001 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363001 1084 #uuid "70de9d14-e9f3-5545-9a7f-d37446be4ff0" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363002 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363003 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363002 1069 "q-12558" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363002 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363002 1071 "$\\int 3x{e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363002 1072 #uuid "708f4971-ac44-5610-9dca-92afa6cd2300" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363002 1074 "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 3x{e}^{2x+5}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{2x+5}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3x\\cdot {e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\int \\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3x{e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3x{e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}\\int {e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3x{e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{3{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363003 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363004 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363003 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363005 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17