$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363037 1072 #uuid "55fb49e6-3301-5747-997a-6aea4f919a61" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363037 1074 "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}xy & =3-{x}^{2}-{y}^{3} \\\\ xy+{x}^{2}+{y}^{3} & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)=xy+{x}^{2}+{y}^{3},$ our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=3.$ \n\nA tangent vector to the level curve that passes through the point $(-1,-1)$ can be computed as follows:\n\n$$\nt(-1,-1)={f}_{y}(-1,-1)i-{f}_{x}(-1,-1)j\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(-1,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy+{x}^{2}+{y}^{3})i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy+{x}^{2}+{y}^{3})j \\\\  & =(x+3{y}^{2})i-(y+2x)j \\\\ t(-1,-1) & =(-1+3(-1)^{2})i-(-1+2(-1))j \\\\  & =2\\,i+3\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our tangent vector is $2\\,i+3\\,j.$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363038 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363039 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363038 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363040 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363038 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363041 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363038 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363042 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363038 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363043 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363038 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363038 1077 "selection" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363038 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363043 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363038 1080 #uuid "d07c4d10-4f15-5f81-9aca-9c05aa1a4821" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363039 1081 "3\\,j" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363039 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363039 1084 #uuid "29f3795a-9c5d-564b-99c5-8234a8f8adae" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363040 1081 "i-2\\,j" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363040 1083 #edb