tible matrix theorem, since $T$ is not invertible, $\\text{rank}(T)\\ne 6.$\n\n- Statement II is false. According to the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{rank}(T)\\ne 6,$ the transformation $T$ is not a bijection.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${{v}_{1}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Ker}(T),$ we must have that $\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{dim(Ker}(T))=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363245 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363246 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363245 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363247 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363245 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363248 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363245 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363249 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363245 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363250 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363245 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363245 1077 "selection" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363245 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363248 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363245 1080 #uuid "36485b72-0685-5aca-a13e-df0bd3457323" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363246 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363246 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363246 1084 #uuid "51b0e2eb-5675-51a7-a8a7-7a545dbb37c8" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363247 1081 "I only" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363247 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363247 1084 #uuid "d0065753-40bf-51c0-a0bd-968981e575e9" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363248 1081 "III only" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363248 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363248 1084 #uuid "2511b99c-93f5-5f2a-a5cd-94c0a9ec2b90" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363249 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533446 175