592186363390 1069 "q-157239" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363390 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363390 1071 "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $5{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3}=0.$\n- ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n- The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly dependent." 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363390 1072 #uuid "cd19f076-6276-574d-a171-58c6f862f950" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363390 1074 "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3} & =5[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+3[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+3[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5-2-3 \\\\ -10+1+9 \\\\ -5-1+6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since statement I is true, we have ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ for ${x}_{1}=5,\\,{x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{3}=3.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is false, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly *dependent*.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 1319