3a" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363397 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363398 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363397 1069 "q-158079" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363397 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363397 1071 "$$\nR\\,=\\,b\n$$\n\nLet $A=QR$  be a QR decomposition of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, and the matrix equation above gives the least-squares solution of $Ax=b.$ From left to right, what are the missing parts of the equation?" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363397 1072 #uuid "a67d6824-3faa-562d-8770-220baba5cc8b" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363397 1074 "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the normal equation\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ R\\,x & ={Q}^{T}\\,b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing parts of the equation are $x$ and ${Q}^{T}.$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363398 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363399 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363398 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363400 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363398 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363401 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363398 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363402 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363398 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363403 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363398 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363398 1077 "selection" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363398 1079 #edb/re