$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363404 1072 #uuid "2664fcbd-5b65-5a40-b14f-fb7042b6173a" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363404 1074 "To get the normal equation corresponding to $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ we pre-multiply both sides of the equation by $(W\\,A)^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot W\\,Ax & =(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot Wb \\\\ {A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)Ax & ={A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n{W}^{T}W=[\\begin{aligned}{1}^{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {3}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & {1}^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nour normal equation can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 9 & -9 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}22 & -8 \\\\ -8 & 11\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the matrix on the left-hand side is invertible, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & ={[\\begin{aligned}11 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 22\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{11\\cdot 22-8\\cdot 8}[\\begin{aligned}11 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 22\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{178}[\\begin{aligned}178 \\\\ 178\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363405 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363406 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363405 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363407 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363405 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363408 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363405 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363409 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363405 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363410 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363405 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363405 1077 "selection" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363405 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363407 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363405 1080 #uuid "b10893fa-4f68-5f42-a725-ae358c74185c" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363406 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363406 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363406 1084 #uuid "bf25468f-d230-53f1-a94f-8f18037a8dfd" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363407 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363407 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363407 1084 #uuid "24438d18-0c67-56f4-8912-fe1ead369af3" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363408 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363408 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363408 1084 #uuid "4bea5562-78d7-5083-8d55-27b52c42ffd2" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363409 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363409 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363409 1084 #uuid "1245d519-bb23-5605-8a30-d545c6f84f82" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363410 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363410 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363410 1084 #uuid "ca976c63-1784-5536-a5ee-be049617b3de" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363411 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363412 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363411 1069 "q-158422" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363411 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363411 1071 "![](images/8f/8f955ee719a4e69f0d09c678f0a74023f137efd7b5ae36d49b98706156384173.png)\n\nConsider the function $f(x)$ whose graph is shown above.\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}x+\\frac{1}{2},\\, & 0<x<1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x$\n- ${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363411 1072 #uuid "ef54c03e-38cc-58aa-92b0-b3a91ad36505" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363411 1074 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. From the graph, we see that $f(x)$ is nonnegative for all $x.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{x}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}]-[\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{0}{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}-0 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statements I and II are true, $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [175921