5 true] [17592186363450 1072 #uuid "507eb77e-f4ca-5d1f-88a7-ae46f550b999" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363450 1074 "We write the position of a point (vector) in spherical polar coordinates as $(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ),$ where \n\n- $\\rho \\ge 0$ is the distance from the point to the origin,\n\n- $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi )$ is the angle between the point and the positive $x$-axis, and\n\n- $ϕ\\in [0,\\pi ]$ is the angle the corresponding vector makes with the positive $z$-axis.\n\nIf $(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)$ are the spherical coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the following formulas:\n\n$$\nx=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,y=\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,z=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\n$$\n\nNotice that the region $R$ represents one-quarter of the sphere of radius $1$ centered at $(0,0,-1).$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write the ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+2z=0$ in spherical polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+2z & =0 \\\\ {\\rho }^{2}+2\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ & =0 \\\\ \\rho (\\rho +2\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $\\rho $ cannot be identical to zero on the entire sphere, we must have $\\rho =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ.$\n\n![](images/14/1499d492c526bad77e81aca1128b6160cc574a209ad7706e8d89b3012112e1df.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that inside our region, the spherical polar coordinates vary within the following domains:\n\n- $\\rho \\in [0,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ]$\n\n- $\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]$\n\n- $ϕ\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ]$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le ϕ\\le \\pi }.\n$$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363451 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363452 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363451 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363453 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363451 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363454 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363451 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363455 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363451 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363456 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363451 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363451 1077 "selection" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363451 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363453 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363451 1080 #uuid "7c562141-9c96-531d-9229-9444719807a8" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363452 1081 "$$\n{(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le ϕ\\le \\pi }\n$$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363452 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363452 1084 #uuid "6cd522c3-15d2-5398-87ca-50c584e203d0" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363453 1081 "$$\n{(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le ϕ\\le \\pi }\n$$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363453 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363453 1084 #uuid "36ac1850-4f78-5af5-8719-57ed661144b0" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363454 1081 "$$\n{(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le ϕ\\le \\pi }\n$$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363454 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363454 1084 #uuid "d752b5b7-69fd-575e-853c-ab8b9a35b184" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363455 1081 "$$\n{(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le ϕ\\le \\pi }\n$$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363455 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533446 175