s gives the critical point $(0,0).$\n\n- Assuming $\\lambda =10$ in the first equation of the system, the second equation of the system implies\n\n$$\n10y=10\\,⇒\\,y=1.\n$$\n\n \nThen, the constraint condition $g(x,y)=0$ implies\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-1=0\\,⇒\\,x=\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the critical points $(\\pm 1,1).$\n\nTherefore, $f$ has possible extreme values at the points\n\n$$\n(0,0),\\,(\\pm 1,1).\n$$\n\nWe evaluate $f$ at each of these points. These are given in the following table:\n\n| $(x,y)$ | $(0,0)$ | $(\\pm 1,1)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x,y)$ | $-3$ | $2$ |\n\nTherefore, the function reaches a maximum value at $(\\pm 1,1),$ and its maximum value is $2.$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363479 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363480 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363479 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363481 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363479 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363482 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363479 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363483 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363479 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363484 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363479 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363479 1077 "selection" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363479 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363482 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363479 1080 #uuid "e6dfd22a-e162-5323-a89b-aa50460a6e68" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363480 1081 "\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363480 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363480 1084 #uuid "0c6956fd-9762-579a-8bc6-7451d5f13355" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363481 1081 "\\frac{2}{5}" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363481 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363481 1084 #uuid "16207e83-a40b-58b6-876e-b124c211c106" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [175921