86 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363506 1071 "Use the method of Lagrange multipliers to find the minimum value of the function $f(x,y,z)=x+y-2z$ on the intersection of the plane $x-2z=2$ and the cylinder ${y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1.$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363506 1072 #uuid "4b5d98c2-fcf8-5024-9f25-b6c4755562d4" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363506 1074 "We need to find the minimum value of \n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=x+y-2z\n$$\n\nsubject to the constraints \n\n$$\ng(x,y,z)=x-2z=2,\\,h(x,y,z)={y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x,y,z)$ is continuous and the constraint is closed and bounded, $f(x,y,z)$ reaches a global maximum and a global minimum on the constraint. \n\nTherefore, by the method of Lagrange multipliers, we must solve the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z)=\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z)+\\mu ∇h(x,y,z) \\\\ g(x,y,z)=2 \\\\ h(x,y,z)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start by expanding the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z)+\\mu ∇h(x,y,z) \\\\ ⟨{f}_{x},{f}_{y},{f}_{z}⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨{g}_{x},{g}_{y},{g}_{z}⟩+\\mu ⟨{h}_{x},{h}_{y},{h}_{z}⟩ \\\\ ⟨1,1,-2⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨1,0,-2⟩+\\mu ⟨0,2y,2z⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}1=\\lambda  \\\\ 1=2\\mu y \\\\ -2=-2\\lambda +2\\mu z\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda =1 \\\\ 1=2\\mu y \\\\ \\mu z=0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\mu $ can't be zero since this leads to a contradiction.  So, from the third equation above, we must have $z=0.$ \n\nNext, we substitute $z=0$ into the first constraint:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-2z & =2 \\\\ x-0 & =2 \\\\ x & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute  $z=0$ into the second constraint:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ y & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $f$ has possible extreme values at the points\n\n$$\n(2,1,0),\\,(2,-1,0).\n$$\n\nWe evaluate $f$ at each of these points. These are given in the following table:\n\n| $(x,y,z)$ | $(2,-1,0)$ | $(2,1,0)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x,y,z)$ | $1$ | $3$ |\n\nTherefore, the function reaches a minimum value at $(2,-1,0),$ and its minimum value is $1.$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363507 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363508 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363507 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363509 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363507 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363510 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363507 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363511 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363507 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363512 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363507 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363507 1077 "selection" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363507 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363510 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363507 1080 #uuid "bfe85ce1-e203-5202-b191-6048438cc5a2" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363508 1081 "3" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363508 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363508 1084 #uuid "580e80e8-6afd-529a-8003-bbf716852f1b" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363509 1081 "2" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363509 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363509 1084 #uuid "85731bde-03bc-52ca-b058-d364ea020e75" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363510 1081 "1" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363510 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363510 1084 #uuid "220b150a-6193-5053-88e3-7215d31c6a92" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363511 1081 "-1" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363511 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363511 1084 #uuid "5b460f4b-ec04-5795-b2a3-60ea7156f962" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [1759