5 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363561 1071 "Let $I=N$ and ${X}_{i}={1,2,…,i},$ then ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}=$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363561 1072 #uuid "7a2f815c-088d-5ada-a242-b2d74124da05" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363561 1074 "The union of a family of indexed sets is the set containing all elements belonging to *at least one* set in the indexed family:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nLet's now write down a few instances of our indexed sets:\n\n- if $i=1,$ we have ${X}_{1}={1}$\n\n- if $i=2,$ we have ${X}_{2}={1,2}$\n\n- if $i=3,$ we have ${X}_{3}={1,2,3}$\n\nand so on. \n\nNotice that ${X}_{i}$ contain all the integers between $1$ and $i.$ So, every natural number $i$ belong to the sets ${X}_{i},\\,{X}_{i+1},\\,{X}_{i+2},…$ \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}=N.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363562 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363563 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363562 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363564 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363562 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363565 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363562 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363566 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363562 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363567 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363562 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363562 1077 "selection" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363562 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363564 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363562 1080 #uuid "0d75f61b-cd99-5293-bfd4-372eef409aff" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363563 1081 "{1}" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363563 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363563 1084 #uuid "646c2dce-0d32-5a34-8e49-d195a2af6e55" 13194139533446 175921860