$ then $f(0.2)=${{field-1}}." 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363575 1072 #uuid "d9e23e70-5782-5a3d-8210-ce965932c28b" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363575 1074 "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $⌈x⌉$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x:$ \n\n$$\n⌈x⌉=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n-1<x\\le n,\\,n\\in Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=0.2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.2) & =(⌈1-2(0.2)⌉+1)^{2} \\\\  & =(⌈1-0.4⌉+1)^{2} \\\\  & =(⌈0.6⌉+1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌈0.6⌉=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.2) & =(⌈0.6⌉+1)^{2} \\\\  & =(1+1)^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363576 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363577 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363576 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363576 1077 "field-1" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363576 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363577 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363576 1080 #uuid "cc5afa72-db25-5e41-89ba-d7b176b3499d" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363577 1081 "4" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363577 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363577 1084 #uuid "66e68199-95ff-538e-bb72-c1d816fb6f3e" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363578 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363579 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363578 1069 "q-182101" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363578 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363578 1071 "Find the value of $f(x)={e}^{⌊8/x⌋}$ at $x=1.5.$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363578 1072 #uuid "0b95e14d-ea28-59e8-91c4-4a46f7550d63" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363578 1074 "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $⌊x⌋$ equals the greatest integer that is less than or equal to $x:$\n\n$$\n⌊x⌋=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n\\le x<n+1,\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=1.5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.5) & ={e}^{⌊8/1.5⌋} \\\\  & ={e}^{⌊5.333…⌋}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌊5.333…⌋=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.5) & ={e}^{⌊5.333…⌋} \\\\  & ={e}^{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363579 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363580 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363579 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363581 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363579 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363582 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363579 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363583 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363579 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363584 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363579 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363579 1077 "selection" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363579 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363580 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363579 1080 #uuid "eb921e22-dea8-50b4-9896-44e025192637" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363580 1081 "{e}^{5}" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363580 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363580 1084 #uuid "983c9bd4-652d-5853-8cbb-1eb77f0162d0" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363581 1081 "{e}^{8}" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363581 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363581 1084 #uuid "ece24300-b25a-5d05-bdde-2f7327327bd8" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363582 1081 "{e}^{6}" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363582 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363582 1084 #uuid "e9fa40b1-7f3c-5af2-bfe5-cbc6820f5ed9" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363583 1081 "{e}^{7}" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363583 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363583 1084 #uuid "dcb09ada-5071-5e33-a3ba-efcdb9dbc49a" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363584 1081 "{e}^{4}" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363584 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363584 1084 #uuid "b761995d-8ff7-56d0-81f9-f3460822afaf" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363585 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363586 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363585 1069 "q-182125" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363585 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363585 1071 "Find the value of $f(x)=x{e}^{⌈x+0.6⌉}$ at $x=1.2.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363585 1072 #uuid "ffa9acea-9036-5826-91e7-bb4d3c63dd63" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363585 1074 "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $⌈x⌉$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x:$ \n\n$$\n⌈x⌉=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n-1<x\\le n,\\,n\\in Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=1.2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.2) & =1.2{e}^{⌈1.2+0.6⌉} \\\\  & =1.2{e}^{⌈1.8⌉}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n⌈1.8⌉=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.2) & =1.2{e}^{⌈1.8⌉} \\\\  & =1.2{e}^{2} \\\\  & =1.2(7.389\\,05…) \\\\  & =8.866\\,86… \\\\  & ≈8.87,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places." 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363586 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363587 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363586 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363588 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363586 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363589 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363586 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363590 13194139533446 17592186