 [17592186363678 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363678 1077 "field-2" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363678 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363679 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363678 1080 #uuid "60e6c9eb-9501-5fab-82a7-68bcc32f55eb" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363679 1081 "25" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363679 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363679 1084 #uuid "d28b6ce6-e19a-50ed-8aa9-2ee67515b28e" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363680 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363681 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363680 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363680 1077 "field-4" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363680 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363681 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363680 1080 #uuid "f6b584b2-296c-5858-8fec-57804a65c614" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363681 1081 "10" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363681 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363681 1084 #uuid "63e1b279-556e-5e29-b829-e24cda7316d9" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363682 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363683 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363682 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363687 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363682 1069 "q-265153" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363682 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363682 1071 "Classify the recurrence relation\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={({a}_{n-1}+{a}_{n-2})}^{2},\\,{a}_{1}=-1,\\,{a}_{2}=2,\\,n\\ge 3.\n$$\n\nThe recurrence relation ${a}_{n}$ has order\n{{field-1}} and\nis\n{{field-2}}." 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363682 1072 #uuid "c65fd905-8c69-5e48-8943-c554e6e881aa" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363682 1074 "Recall the following classifications of recurrence relations:\n\n- The order of a relation ${a}_{n}$ is the largest index difference between ${a}_{n}$ and the preceding terms in the relation.\n\n- A recurrence relation is *linear (with constant coefficients)* if it expresses ${a}_{n}$ as a sum of previous terms ${a}_{n-1},…,{a}_{n-k}$ with constant coefficients, together with possibly a final term that depends only on $n:$\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={s}_{1}{a}_{n-1}+{s}_{2}{a}_{n-2}+…+{s}_{k}{a}_{n-k}+g(n)\n$$\n\nwhere ${s}_{1},{s}_{2},…,{s}_{k}$ are constants and $g(n)$ is a function, often called a *forcing function*, that does not involve ${a}_{n}$ or its preceding terms.\n\n- A linear recurrence relation (with constant coefficients) is *homogeneous* if the forcing function is zero. Otherwise, it is *inhomogeneous.*\n\nLet's classify the relation ${a}_{n}={({a}_{n-1}+{a}_{n-2})}^{2}.$\n\n- The largest index difference between ${a}_{n}$ and the preceding terms ${a}_{n-1}$ and ${a}_{n-2}$ in the relation is $2.$ So, the relation has order $2.$\n\n- Since ${({a}_{n-1}+{a}_{n-2})}^{2}={a}_{n-1}^{2}+2{a}_{n-1}{a}_{n-2}+{a}_{n-2}^{2},$ the terms ${a}_{n-1}$ and ${a}_{n-2}$ are not in the first power. So, the relation is non-linear.\n\nTherefore, the recurrence relation ${a}_{n}$ has order\n$2$ and is\n$\\text{non-linear}.$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363683 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363684 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363683 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363685 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363683 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363686 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363683 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363683 1077 "field-1" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363683 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363685 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363683 1080 #uuid "8b14f30b-f9bb-576d-951d-2015d26afb89" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363684 1081 "3" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363684 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 175921860