or $t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ where $t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363690 1072 #uuid "fd51ce8b-a6c3-539b-9695-7b0017ded9ff" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363690 1074 "The parametric equations of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=\\sqrt{4}=2$ and $b=\\sqrt{3}.$ Therefore, the parametric equations are\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363691 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363692 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363691 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363691 1077 "field-1" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363691 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363692 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363691 1080 #uuid "5c997a8a-bf0e-504d-a0f7-0b801fd4789c" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363692 1081 "\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}t" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363692 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363692 1084 #uuid "885de1b1-5af8-5777-ac30-68bacef5a7e0" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363693 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363694 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363693 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363696 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363693 1069 "q-275798" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363693 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363693 1071 "![](images/da/daada2a7ad84b9f6db82706ad16da02a9b3cba329e56ced53d6b99b5852751ca.png)\n\nOne branch of a hyperbola (shown above) is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$\n\nDetermine the domain of the parameter $t$ for this branch, assuming that the entire hyperbola is defined only for $t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ].$\n\n$t\\in (${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$)$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363693 1072 #uuid "da3d1309-df8f-5429-a584-56e05f4428ef" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363693 1074 "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a single branch, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](images/21/212e8525a548d21774fec50b87ea34f368ac5821176b86859c14b1bfcef74407.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ we get only the upper branch.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe only the upper branch are\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).\n$$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363694 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363695 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363694 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363694 1077 "field-1" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363694 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363695 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363694 1080 #uuid "8c0e8be6-f8bd-5e6c-9640-2eb665d0c6d7" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363695 1081 "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363695 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363695 1084 #uuid "2090ebe8-0607-5bcd-914e-d9889e659d81" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363696 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363697 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363696 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363696 1077 "field-2" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363696 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363697 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363696 1080 #uuid "c28cc473-ed96-5f12-98fc-5b27c6f28539" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363697 1081 "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363697 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363697 1084 #uuid "c24b9854-a092-5362-932a-05741ab5e96f" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363698 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363699 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363698 1069 "q-302305" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363698 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363698 1071 "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 49}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-7}{x-49}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363698 1072 #uuid "6335e79e-5245-5d37-9e43-3b02d69d8f54" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363698 1074 "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 49}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-7}{x-49} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{49}-7}{49-49}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 49}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-7}{x-49} & ={lim}_{x\\to 49}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x}-7)(\\sqrt{x}+7)}{(x-49)(\\sqrt{x}+7)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 49}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x})^{2}-{7}^{2}}{(x-49)(\\sqrt{x}+7)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 49}\\frac{x-49}{(x-49)(\\sqrt{x}+7)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 49}\\frac{\\cancel{x-49}}{\\cancel{(x-49)}(\\sqrt{x}+7)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 49}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}+7} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{49}+7} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7+7} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363699 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363700 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363699 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363699 1077 "field-1" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363699 1079 #e