lar solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=7x{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nNow, since the general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nthe general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{x}+7x{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nWe can find the constant $A$ using the initial conditions.\n\nSubstituting $y(0)=4$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+0 & =4 \\\\ A & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=4{e}^{x}+7x{e}^{x}.\n$$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363749 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363750 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363749 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363749 1077 "field-1" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363749 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363750 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363749 1080 #uuid "7bffb413-d127-5384-b66a-53461a8d5549" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363750 1081 "4{e}^{x}+7x{e}^{x}" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363750 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363750 1084 #uuid "c009c47c-0010-58f0-af3f-4c58afce7657" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363751 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363752 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363751 1069 "q-333028" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363751 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363751 1071 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}-3y=3{x}^{2}-2x+1,\\,y(0)=2\n$$\n\nGiven that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}-3y=3{x}^{2}-2x+1\n$$\n\nhas the complementary solution ${y}_{c}=A{e}^{3x},$ solve the initial value problem." 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363751 1072 #uuid "1b51285c-c91c-5b59-9669-57cdf45b6f8d" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186363751 1074 "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and par