as at most one solution if and only if the associated homogeneous BVP has only the trivial solution $y≡0.$ \n\nTo find the solution of an inhomogeneous boundary value problem (BVP):\n\n- First, we find the general solution ${y}_{h}(x)$ of the corresponding homogeneous equation.\n\n- Then, we find a particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ of the inhomogeneous equation.\n\n- Finally, we apply the boundary conditions to determine the arbitrary constants.\n\nThe homogeneous equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+y=0.\n$$\n\nTo find the fundamental solutions, we set $y={e}^{mx}.$ The auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}-2m+1 & =0 \\\\ (m-1)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a repeated root $m=1.$ So, the fundamental solutions are \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(x)={e}^{x},\\,{y}_{2}(x)=x{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the homogeneous equation is\n\n$$\n{y}_{h}=(A+Bx){e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nNow, we seek a particular solution ${y}_{p}$ of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=D.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our inhomogeneous equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(D)^{″}-2(D)^{′}+(D) & =4 \\\\ D & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=4\n$$\n\nand the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={y}_{h}+{y}_{p} \\\\  & =(A+Bx){e}^{x}+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =(A+B(x+1)){e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the condition ${y}^{′}(-1)=0$ gives\n\n$$\nA{e}^{-1}=0\\,⇒\\,A=0.\n$$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=B(x+1){e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nApplying the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(0+1){e}^{0} & =1\\,⇒\\,B=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, for the function $g(x),$ we have\n\n$$\ng(x)={y}_{p}(x)=4.\n$$\n\n**Note**: The associated homogeneous BVP\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+y=0,\\,{y}^{′}(-1)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0,\\,-1\\le x\\le 0\n$$\n\nhas only the trivial solution $y≡0.$ Therefore, the inhomogeneous BVP has at most one solution. Since we have found a solution satisfying both boundary conditions, the solution to this inhomogeneous BVP is unique." 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364021 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364022 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364021 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364023 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364021 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364024 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364021 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364021 1077 "field-2" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364021 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364022 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364021 1080 #uuid "8ef46b8a-d1f4-5a26-8e97-431e4b16b69d" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364022 1081 "1" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364022 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364022 1084 #uuid "83dda7a3-eacb-529f-adbb-afa7998482a3" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364023 1081 "0" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364023 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364023 1084 #uuid "b6f9c32e-0d33-567a-b97d-bcf77bc79762" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364024 1081 "-2" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364024 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364024 1084 #uuid "46ce2673-4c7c-54c8-a559-71bbc18c3e45" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364025 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364026 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364025 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364027 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364025 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364028 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364025 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364025 1077 "field-1" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364025 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364027 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364025 1080 #uuid "3b68c1eb-130b-57da-9d11-65409dd2f78c" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [175921