 [17592186364091 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364091 1084 #uuid "18e59bd2-e03b-552f-863d-b8b11dece63e" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364092 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364092 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364092 1084 #uuid "5963827a-77af-5e33-8fb7-88cec4f8cee9" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364093 1081 "I only" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364093 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364093 1084 #uuid "b1237451-9ef4-5d27-a387-a8ffc30e76bf" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364094 1081 "III only" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364094 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364094 1084 #uuid "715a376f-1d79-5e2b-8c66-84c45b380852" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364095 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364095 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364095 1084 #uuid "caa27d7c-d57f-538d-bd6d-16b9baa97d4d" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364096 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364097 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364096 1069 "q-346044" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364096 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364096 1071 "Given that ${\\int }_{7}^{2}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-9,$ calculate \n${\\int }_{2}^{7}(-3f(x)+6)\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\n${\\int }_{2}^{7}(-3f(x)+6)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364096 1072 #uuid "9eecce94-cbc9-5815-b3a1-79f3d550fe1a" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364096 1074 "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{7}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{7}^{2}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{7}(-3f(x)+6)\\,\\text{d}x & =-3{\\int }_{2}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,6{\\int }_{2}^{7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3(9)\\,+\\,6\\cdot x\\,{|}_{2}^{7} \\\\  & =-27\\,+\\,6(7-2) \\\\  & =-27\\,+\\,30 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364097 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364098 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364097 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364097 1077 "field-1" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364097 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364098 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364097 1080 #uuid "a11f1144-0b76-5319-af8c-eda04eab9424" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364098 1081 "3" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364098 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364098 1084 #uuid "714e8799-59e0-581a-9991-8b466b5d4554" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364099 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364100 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364099 1069 "q-346049" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364099 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364099 1071 "A logistics manager tracks the total distance $s$, in kilometers, traveled by a delivery drone. The following table shows the drone’s speed.\n\n| **$t\\,\\text{(minutes)}$** | $5$ | $10$ | $15$ | $20$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${s}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{(km/min)}$ | $0.42$ | $0.48$ | $0.53$ | $0.58$ |\n\nAt $t=10,$ the drone had traveled $4.6$ kilometers. Use the tangent line approximation of $s$ at time $t=10$ to estimate the distance traveled at $t=11.$  Do not round the answer.\n\nThe distance traveled by the drone at $t=11$ minutes is estimated to be\n{{field-1}}\nkilometers." 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364099 1072 #uuid "60dc0e80-53b0-557f-a4fc-ea79525020cb" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364099 1074 "The tangent line approximation of $s(t)$ at the point $a=10$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(t) & =s(a)+{s}^{′}(a)(t-a) \\\\  & =s(10)+{s}^{′}(10)(t-10) \\\\  & =4.6+0.48(t-10).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $s(11)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $t=11.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s(11) & ≈L(11) \\\\  & =4.6+0.48(11-10) \\\\  & =4.6+0.48(1) \\\\  & =4.6+0.48 \\\\  & =5.08.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe distance traveled by the drone at $t=11$ minutes is estimated to be $5.08$ kilometers." 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364100 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364101 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364100 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364100 1077 "field-1" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364100 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364101 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364100 1080 #uuid "7ab52d47-3aa1-586f-bcb5-3e2b8a69f93d" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364101 1081 "5.08" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364101 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364101 1084 #uuid "554f3ed2-3d6e-563f-9468-f8e5cccf4659" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364102 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364103 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364102 1069 "q-346183" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364102 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364102 1071 "Given that ${\\int }_{2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=4$ and ${\\int }_{5}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-6,$ \nthen what is ${\\int }_{2}^{9}(3-2f(x))\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{2}^{9}(3-2f(x))\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364102 1072 #uuid "ea13ab41-3765-5b90-820d-c19bfc25be2b" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364102 1074 "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{5}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,=\\,{\\int }_{2}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information gives\n\n$$\n4+(-6)\\,=\\,{\\int }_{2}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,⇒\\,{\\int }_{2}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-2.\n$$\n\nFinally, compute the desired integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{9}(3-2f(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{2}^{9}1\\,\\text{d}x\\,-\\,2{\\int }_{2}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\cdot x{|}_{2}^{9}\\,-\\,2(-2) \\\\  & =3(9-2)+4 \\\\  & =21+4 \\\\  & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364103 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364104 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364103 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364103 1077 "field-1" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364103 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364104 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364103 1080 #uuid "9ce55b42-1f81-52e3-ac6c-85adce4e86bb" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364104 1081 "25" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364104 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364104 1084 #uuid "8ff278a7-a902-5ef3-b222-642dcf4997fd" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364105 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364106 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364105 1069 "q-346196" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364105 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364105 1071 "Given that ${\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-6$ and ${\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=8,$ \nthen what is ${\\int }_{-1}^{5}(2f(x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{-1}^{5}(2f(x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364105 1072 #uuid "9a175642-dffe-5ca1-aaf0-cc3658908d92" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364105 1074 "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information gives\n\n$$\n(-6)+8={\\int }_{-1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,⇒\\,{\\int }_{-1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=2.\n$$\n\nFinally, compute the desired integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{5}(2f(x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{-1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{5}1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(2)+x\\,{|}_{-1}^{5} \\\\  & =4+(5-(-1)) \\\\  & =4+6 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364106 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364107 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364106 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364106 1077 "field-1" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364106 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364107 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364106 1080 #uuid "c8456bda-8637-5bee-8eeb-c0797634e6a8" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364107 1081 "10" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364107 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364107 1084 #uuid "68181419-8946-5442-8e35-bab9116d8715" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364108 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364109 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364108 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364115 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364108 1069 "q-346711" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364108 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364108 1071 "The graph of the function $y=f(x)$ passes through $(3,5)$ and is concave down on the interval $(2,5).$ If ${f}^{′}(3)=2,$ estimate the value of $f(2.6)$ using the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=3$ and determine whether the approximation is an underestimate or overestimate.$\\,f(2.6)≈$ {{field-1}} and the approximation is an {{field-2}}." 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364108 1072 #uuid "251c3f14-67be-5ce8-94e8-62c33b59ad09" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364108 1074 "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $a=3$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\