ve that\n\n$$\nT({v}_{1})=T({v}_{2})\\,⟹\\,T({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since ${v}_{1}-{v}_{2}\\in \\text{Ker}(T)$ and ${v}_{1}\\ne {v}_{2},$ we must have that $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {0}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. According to the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {0},$ the transformation $T$ and the matrix $T$ are not invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $T$ is not invertible, the invertible matrix theorem implies that $\\text{nullity}(T)\\ne 0.$ In turn, this means that $\\text{nullity}(T)>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364152 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364153 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364152 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364154 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364152 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364155 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364152 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364156 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364152 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364157 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364152 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364152 1077 "selection" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364152 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364156 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364152 1080 #uuid "ea5cc0e6-6d5a-59ee-82ed-ff12bda5ecf8" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364153 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364153 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364153 1084 #uuid "b5f07bf4-4a80-5c38-8806-6cbd8d26fa57" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364154 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364154 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364154 1084 #uuid "862b97ed-b399-5806-9f72-3a71bd6e9f7f" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364155 1081 "I only" 13194139533446 17