)\\ne {R}^{3}.$ Therefore, according to the Invertible Matrix Theorem, we must have $\\text{nullity}(T)\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{Im}(T)\\ne {R}^{3}$, then $\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)\\ne 3.$\n\n- Statement III is false. According to the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{Im}(T)\\ne {R}^{3},$ the transformation $T$ can't be a bijection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364220 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364221 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364220 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364222 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364220 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364223 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364220 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364224 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364220 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364225 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364220 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364220 1077 "selection" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364220 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364223 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364220 1080 #uuid "ad2b2b69-4210-5e1c-81b8-a09e94838b9f" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364221 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364221 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364221 1084 #uuid "c52cc7b6-9bfa-5536-9e5f-59eeb0900797" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364222 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364222 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364222 1084 #uuid "b4ecdf86-13ef-5e0a-b4f9-6f8533300313" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364223 1081 "I only" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364223 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364223 1084 #uuid "9ed48d52-d008-59d3-a693-7857aac6b5e6" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364224 1081 "I and II only" 13