rue] [17592186364230 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364230 1084 #uuid "a1dec09d-6d2d-523d-9089-bf241635b1d7" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364231 1081 "4" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364231 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364231 1084 #uuid "d27fe663-f807-596b-a3ce-069f50d69d3b" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364232 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364233 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364232 1069 "q-4814" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364232 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364232 1071 "Let $f$ be a function such that ${f}^{′}(x)=12{x}^{2}-6$ and $f(1)=-2.$ Use the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=1$ to estimate the value of $f(2).$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364232 1072 #uuid "7c05a076-435e-50b5-bc51-d3ae092e8ee4" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364232 1074 "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $a=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(1)+{f}^{′}(1)(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that $f(1)=-2,$ and since ${f}^{′}(x)=12{x}^{2}-6,$ then ${f}^{′}(1)=12(1)^{2}-6=6.$ So, the tangent line approximation is given by\n\n$$\nL(x)=-2+6(x-1).\n$$\n\nNow, we can approximate $f(2)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=2.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) & ≈L(2) \\\\  & =-2+6(2-1) \\\\  & =-2+6(1) \\\\  & =-2+6 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364233 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364234 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364233 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364235 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364233 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364236 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364233 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364237 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364233 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364238 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [175921