17592186045585 true] [17592186364308 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364308 1071 "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(1,1,0)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n$r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364308 1072 #uuid "091b9ad4-6dc4-5677-b067-721682dcc589" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364308 1074 "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨1,1,0⟩.$ From the vectorial equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨-2,-3,1⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨-2,-3,1⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,1⟩ & =⟨1,1,0⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,1⟩ & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,1⟩ & =-5 \\\\ -2x-3y+z & =-5 \\\\ -2x-3y+z+5 & =0 \\\\ 2x+3y-z-5 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364309 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364310 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364309 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364311 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364309 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364312 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364309 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364313 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364309 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364314 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364309 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364309 1077 "selection" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364309 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364313 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364309 1080 #uuid "8e8ea1c7-6edb-564b-ac95-d5d2b72cd2e1" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [1759218636431