n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 12 & -9 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -8 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -8 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-4z=3 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove these equations from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\nx+2y-4z=3\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables $y$ and $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y,z.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\nx=3-2y+4z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3-2y+4z \\\\ y=y \\\\ z=z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y,z$ (the free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3-2y+4z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364351 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364352 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364351 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364353 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364351 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364354 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364351 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364355 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364351 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364356 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364351 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364351 1077 "selection" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364351 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364356 1319