7592186045585 true] [17592186364398 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364398 1071 "Let $f$ be a function such that ${f}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}}$ and $f(9)=-10.$ Use the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=9$ to estimate the value of $f(8.7).$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364398 1072 #uuid "7d2c4ba1-9d35-536b-bfbf-3ccc7aa1bc93" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364398 1074 "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $a=9$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(9)+{f}^{′}(9)(x-9).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that $f(9)=-10,$ and since ${f}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}},$ then ${f}^{′}(9)=-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{9}}=-\\frac{2}{3}.$ So, the tangent line approximation is given by\n\n$$\nL(x)=-10-\\frac{2}{3}(x-9).\n$$\n\nNow, we can approximate $f(8.7)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=8.7.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(8.7) & ≈L(8.7) \\\\  & =-10-\\frac{2}{3}(8.7-9) \\\\  & =-10-\\frac{2}{3}(-0.3) \\\\  & =-10+0.2 \\\\  & =-9.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364399 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364400 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364399 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364401 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364399 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364402 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364399 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364403 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364399 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364404 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364399 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364399 1077 "selection" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364399 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364403 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364399 1080 #uuid "11182bd3-4c4a-5657-b0f0-5ff8daad0025" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364400 1081 "-10.4" 13194139533446 17592186045585 true] [17592186364400 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533446 1759218